Q: Making PHP var_dump() values display one line per value A: <p>I had a different solution that fixed it for me so I could store the information in an array instead of just printing it out. In my case the difficulty was it was only returning a single row when looking for my table schema while writing a function for update queries while I was making a console for my DB.</p>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>$tables = &quot;SELECT TABLE_NAME FROM information_schema.TABLES WHERE TABLE_SCHEMA = 'table_name';&quot;;
$info = search($tables);
$rows=mysqli_num_rows($info);
for($i=0;$i&lt;$rows;$i++){
    $total[] = mysqli_fetch_assoc($info);
}
var_dump($total);
</code></pre>
